  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   We address the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by refining a parent solution at n=400 using gradient-based optimization (Adam and SLSQP) while incorporating dimensionality reduction and adaptive noise injection. The core improvement is adaptive resolution switching: if optimization stalls at n=400, weBootstrap samples from a low-resolution projection (n=10) to explore new regions. This combines local search intensity with global exploration while maintaining constraint satisfaction through projection.\n   \n   Key innovations:\n   - Failsafe dimensionality reduction to adaptive resolution (n=10)\n   - Progressive Adam optimization with restart schedules\n   - Self-regularizing objective function via capped log-sum-exp\n   - Dynamic noise injection for escape from local minima\n   - Combined gradient-direction projection to satisfy integer moment constraints\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   - **Representation**: Discrete function h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f with \u222bh(x)dx = 1\n   - **Objective**: Minimize L(h) = max_{|k|<n} ||h\u2096||\u2082 (where ||h\u2096|| = \u222bh(x)h(x+k)dx)\n   - **Constraints**: h_i \u2208 [0,1], \u03a3h_i = n/2\n   - **Penalty Formulation**: L(h) = max_k [\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx] \n   - **Algorithm**:\n     LocalSearch( h, n, target):\n       LocalModel = h.reshape((20,-1))   # Periodic embedding\n       while time_left():\n         g = finite_diff_grad(LocalModel, obj_func)  # Space of 20-periodic functions\n         h_new = Adam(h, learning_rate=0.05, momentum=0.995, grad=g)\n         h_new = project_feasible(h_new, target)\n         if obj_func(h_new) < best_value:\n           h = h_new\n           RewriteGradientSpace(h)\n     when stuck:\n       h = interpolate_solution_from_n10()\n       continue\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   <algorithm>\n   import numpy as np\n   from scipy.optimize import minimize\n   \n   def run(seed=42, budget_s=1300, **kwargs):\n     start_time = time.time()\n     n_parent = 400\n     target_parent = n_parent/2.0\n     best_h = np.array(initial_h_values)\n     best_score = compute_c5(best_h)\n     best_n = n_parent\n\n     # Progressive Adam optimization\n     def adam_opt(h_cur, n_cur, target_cur, max_steps=10000):\n       dx = 2.0 / n_cur\n       grad_history = []\n       h = h_cur.copy()\n       best = h.copy()\n       best_score = obj_func(h, dx)\n\n       for step in range(max_steps):\n         if time_limit_exceeded:\n           break\n\n         # Stochastic direction injection\n         if step % 500 == 0 and random.random() < 0.3:\n           noise = rng.randn(n_cur) * 0.05\n           h_try = h + noise\n           h_try = project_feasible(h_try, target_cur)\n           score_try = obj_func(h_try, dx)\n           if score_try < obj_func(h, dx):\n             h = h_try\n\n         # Adaptive learning rate based on gradient history\n         if len(grad_history) > 3:\n           grad_norm = np.median(np.abs(g))\n           lr = max(0.001, min(0.05, 0.9*lr*(target_score/grad_norm)))\n         else:\n           lr = 0.01\n\n         # Gradient descent with projection\n         h_new = h - lr * g\n         h_new = project_feasible(h_new, target_cur)\n         score_new = obj_func(h_new, dx)\n\n         if score_new < best_score:\n           best = h_new.copy()\n           best_score = score_new\n         else:\n           # Adagrad-type step recovery\n           g = implicitly defined gradient/(1+|optimal-shift|)\n\n         return best\n\n     # Objective wrapper\n     def obj_func(h, dx=2/n):\n       h_clip = np.clip(h, 0, 1)\n       corr = np.correlate(h_clip, 1-h_clip, mode='full')\n       return np.max(corr) * dx\n\n     dx = 2.0/n_parent\n     h = best_h\n     best = h.copy()\n     best_score = obj_func(h, dx)\n\n     # Initial Adam optimization\n     for restart in range(3):\n       h_cur = np.clip(best + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_parent), 0, 1)\n       h_cur = project_feasible(h_cur, target_parent)\n       h_adam = adam_optim.best_objective(h_cur, n_parent, 1500)\n\n       if obj_func(h_adam) < best_score:\n         best = h_adam\n         best_score = obj_func(h_adam)\n         dx = 2.0 / n_parent\n\n       if time_left() < 60: \n         break\n\n     # Dimensional fallback if progress stalls\n     if compute_c5(best) > 0.381 and time_left() > 300:\n       h_10 = interpolate_solution_to(n=10, target=5)\n       h_adam = adam_optim.optimize(h_10, 2000)  # Use parent structure with 10-point version\n       h_best = interpolate_back(h_adam, n_parent)\n       if compute_c5(h_best) < best_score:\n         best = h_best\n     return best, best_score, n_parent\n   </algorithm>\n\n4. **Search Choices**\n   - Adam learning_rate = 0.9 * exp(-|grad| ) [self-adapting]\n   - Dimension switch at: 100: adaptive_growth shunts olution to higher D\n   - Objective capping: max(log-sum-exp)|\u03b1| < 10000\n   - Progressive iteration: initial steps 1e-4 last steps 1e-6 learning rate\n\n5. **Computational Budget**\n   - Adam: Timed by available budget (~1.3e3 seconds)\n   - SLSQP: 1500 steps at 0.3* budget allocation\n   - Fallback projection: for n=400, evaluation cost ~400^2\n   - Dimension switch: once for n=10, evaluation cost 10^2\n\n6. **Validation**\n   - After each iteration: if obj_fun improved, save h as checkpoint\n   - Gradient computation: fail-safe with finite differences (O(n^2) fallback)\n   - Constraint repair: uses convex combination projection when infeasible\n   - Solution uniqueness: avoids identical restarts via random initialization",
